WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.701
-Today is Friday.

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.901
Happy Friday, everyone.

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:05.972
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:05.972 --> 00:00:09.042
Friday is when I usually
catch up on some personal stuff,

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.209
I got to be honest.
You know,

00:00:10.209 --> 00:00:11.811
I check my inbox,

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.146
only on Fridays...
-Right.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.213
[ Laughter ]
-...and return some emails

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:15.215
and, of course, I send out

00:00:15.215 --> 00:00:16.482
thank-you notes every week.

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:18.518
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.953
I was running a bit
behind today, so I thought,

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.688
if you guys wouldn't mind,
I'd like to write out

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:22.989
my weekly thank-you notes
right now.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.089
Is that okay with you guys?

00:00:24.089 --> 00:00:25.457
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:26.926
-Wow.
Very nice of them.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.229
-James, can you give me

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:30.763
some thank-you note writing
music, please?

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.165
-[ Playing tender tune ]

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:35.935
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:39.105
It's got a good jam to it.
-Yeah. Mm.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:40.540
♪♪

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.743
-Thank you, Blue Origin
space flight team,

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.578
for looking like you took
your official photo

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:46.912
at a Sears Portrait Studio.

00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:49.983
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:53.419 --> 00:00:54.854
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:58.858
Thank you, residents of the town
in "Halloween" movies,

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.760
for continuing to live there,
even though there's been

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:03.730
a festive slasher on the loose
for 40 years.

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:07.300
[ Laughter, cheering,
and applause ]

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.768
How bad could it --
-Yeah.

00:01:08.768 --> 00:01:10.069
-This could be the year
he doesn't?

00:01:10.069 --> 00:01:11.637
-"This house only costs
$10,000."

00:01:11.637 --> 00:01:13.839
[ Laughter ]
-"They'll give us $10,000?"

00:01:13.839 --> 00:01:16.276
-Yeah, to live there.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.811
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:21.347
-Thank you, people who leave out
a bowl of candy on Halloween,

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.916
for basically saying, "I'm sure
you look funny or scary,

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:26.318
or whatever. Just take a Twix
and get off my property."

00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:29.355
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:30.457
"I'm over it.
I'm over it."

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.660
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.729
Thank you, patio heaters,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.797
for coming in two styles --
street lamp

00:01:38.797 --> 00:01:40.365
and Indiana Jones Temple.

00:01:40.365 --> 00:01:42.936
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:43.970
I feel like I'm on vacation.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.304
-I know.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.304 --> 00:01:46.472
I didn't know they were Irish.

00:01:46.472 --> 00:01:48.007
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:49.309
Paddy O'Heaters.
[patio heaters]

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:52.278
[ Laughter ]

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:00.319
-Oh, my gosh.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:02.088
-Who are you thanking now?
-What's that?

00:02:02.088 --> 00:02:03.489
[ Laughter ]

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:04.857
-Who are you thanking now?
-I write out thank-you notes.

00:02:04.857 --> 00:02:07.193
I put them in the envelope
and they get sent to the...

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.195
-The people who you thank.
-...the proper -- yeah.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.329
-People, yeah.
-Correct.

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:12.432
Or things or --
-Or whole towns.

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.066
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, so, this one, I think,

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:16.336
you'll really enjoy.
-I'm waiting for it.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.470
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.839
-I think you will.

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.774
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.075
♪♪

00:02:23.075 --> 00:02:24.843
Thank you, Saran Wrap,

00:02:24.843 --> 00:02:27.013
for always being
one small tug away

00:02:27.013 --> 00:02:28.580
from being completely useless.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.684
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.921
-Is this the last one?
-No.

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:35.989
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:37.990
♪♪
-Thank you,

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.592
Mellowcreme Pumpkins,

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:42.528
for being candy corn that went
into Witness Protection Program.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:43.997
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.098
That's a goodie.

00:02:47.867 --> 00:02:49.902
-Mmm, candy corn.
-Yep.

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:51.070
Here we go.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.472
♪♪
Thank you, haystacks,

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.841
for letting people decorate
their house with horse food.

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:57.009
There you have it, everybody.
[ Cheering and applause ]

00:02:57.009 --> 00:02:58.444
Those are thank-you notes!

